# What `mcpb pack` leaves out of the MCP Bundle (gitignore syntax).
#
# An allowlist, not a denylist: everything at the top level is excluded and
# only what the server needs at runtime is let back in. A denylist would ship
# any file nobody thought to list — a local .env, the registry tokens
# (.mcpregistry_*), test fixtures — into a file that gets published.
#
# node_modules must hold production dependencies only (npm ci --omit=dev);
# scripts/verify-mcpb.js fails a bundle that contains a dev dependency.

/*
!/manifest.json
!/package.json
!/LICENSE
!/PRIVACY.md
!/README.md
!/src
!/node_modules
